A process's description tells PROCESS_REGION_SLOTS as the regions it may have installed,
where the PMP has fewer entries for them, as RP2350's Hazard3 has seven.

Caught-by: fuzz-rp2350
Report: a description differs from the capability it describes

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -936,7 +936,7 @@ static __attribute__((noinline)) int cap_info(const struct cap *cap, uint32_t *a
         break;
     case CAP_PROCESS:
         /* What process_install holds an install to: a slot each, and an entry each. */
-        arg[2] = pmp_entry_count < PROCESS_REGION_SLOTS ? pmp_entry_count : PROCESS_REGION_SLOTS;
+        arg[2] = PROCESS_REGION_SLOTS;
         break;
     case CAP_NOTIFICATION:
         /* The bits it may signal, never those that are set, which only a wait takes, with RIGHT_R. */
